          what: 'Adds sub-regional ridges and ravines whose crests follow the contour lines of the terrain, which plain noise does not do. It is an optional detail on either preset and changes the physical heights.',
          algo: 'A GPU adaptation of phasor noise as used for terrain amplification (Tricard et al. 2019; Grenier et al. 2024): each octave sums jittered Gabor impulses, z = sum w_j exp(i phase_j), with carrier directions along the regional contour tangent, and a bounded triangle-like profile (2/pi) asin(Re z / sqrt(|z|^2 + eps)). At most three octaves, wavelength ratio 3, base wavelength clamp(scale/24, 48, 160) m; amplitude min(0.025 wavelength, 0.12 slope wavelength) fading on flat ground, valley floors and near sea level. Wavelengths below four output cells are suppressed.',
          io: 'In: surface heights and slope. Out: heights plus detail.',
          ctl: 'Phasor intensity (zero turns it off).',
          perf: 'Fused into the final output-packing dispatch, so it needs no full-size intermediate texture. At 50 km most small octaves are absent because they fall below the cell size. The detail is not a drainage network that was physically evolved.',
